{"name":"Golden Slumber","hex":"#b98841","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"slumber","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very light state of sleep, almost awake.\n\n A very heavy state of sleep.","A very heavy state of sleep."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be in a very light state of sleep, almost awake.","To be inactive or negligent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slumber"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden Slumber","blocks":[{"text":"Golden Slumber is a 2018 South Korean action thriller film directed by Noh Dong-seok, starring Gang Dong-won, Kim Eui-sung, Kim Sung-kyun, Kim Dae-myung, Han Hyo-joo and Yoon Kye-sang. It is based on the 2007 Japanese novel of the same name written by Kōtarō Isaka, previously filmed by Yoshihiro Nakamura in 2010. The film revolves around a deliveryman who has to run for his life after he is held responsible for an explosion causing the death of a presidential candidate."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0f/Golden_Slumber_%28%EA%B3%A8%EB%93%A0%EC%8A%AC%EB%9F%BC%EB%B2%84%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Slumber","wikidata":"Q29650253"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold